# ChibiSprites: character art from finalbossblues' free Asset Alliance
# chibi sets (itch.io, 16-char collection), converted to code so the
# project stays plain text and pushable (no PNG files in the repo).
# Each frame is 16x32, stored as a colour palette plus rows of
# single characters: '.' is transparent, any other character is an
# index into that frame's palette. Frames are upscaled 2x with
# nearest-neighbour, so they render at 32x64 in-game.
#
# Character picks (RPGMaker charset blocks):
#   player = charsetA, column 4, row 2 (red cap, yellow shirt)
#   shopkeeper = charsetA, column 1, row 2 (black suit)
#   storage_keeper = charsetB, column 4, row 1 (blue hat)
#   elder = charsetA, column 4, row 1 (brown coat)
#   villagers (SetC/expansion): bram = charsetC, column 4, row 1
#     (bearded man); mira = charsetC, column 1, row 2 (blond girl);
#     kaze = charsetC, column 4, row 2 (ninja)
# To swap a character, re-extract a different block and replace
# that character's frames here.
class_name ChibiSprites
extends RefCounted

